 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "The staff are hungry, and Max is in charge of lunch. Senya asks when it will be ready, and Max promises a special soup that is nothing like the usual slop. Here's the Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Макс, мы сегодня обедать будем?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Конечно, всё уже почти готово!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Мы все очень хотим есть.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Подождите ещё пару минут.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Что ты нам приготовил сегодня?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я сварил особенный суп-пюре.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Обычный суп был бы лучше.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Вы все пальчики оближете!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Надеюсь, это можно есть.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Вы такого никогда не пробовали.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Главное, чтобы было вкусно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Это не то обычное месиво.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Ладно, неси скорее на стол!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Сейчас я вас всех удивлю!",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now the wait for lunch.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Макс, мы сегодня обедать будем?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Max, are we going to have lunch today?' The Russian expression for 'to have lunch' is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "обедать",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", built from lunch. Senya puts it before ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "будем?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning we will, which stresses the lunch.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Конечно, всё уже почти готово!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Of course, everything is already almost ready!' The Russian term for 'almost' is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "почти",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "готово!",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " matches the shape of ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "всё",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning everything.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Мы все очень хотим есть.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We all really want to eat.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "хотим есть.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'we want to eat', which is the usual phrase for 'we're hungry'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Подождите ещё пару минут.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Wait a couple more minutes.' The Russian expression for 'wait' aimed at several people is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Подождите",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "ещё пару минут.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'another couple of minutes'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Что ты нам приготовил сегодня?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What did you prepare for us today?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "нам",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", literally 'to us', does the job of 'for us'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "приготовил",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'prepared' when said of a man.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я сварил особенный суп-пюре.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I cooked a special purée soup.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "сварил",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is built from the action word for boil, with a prefix showing it is finished. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "суп-пюре.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is a borrowed combination.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Обычный суп был бы лучше.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'A regular soup would be better.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "бы",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the little word for 'would', so ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "был бы лучше.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'would be better'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Вы все пальчики оближете!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You will all lick your fingers!' A cook's promise: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "пальчики оближете!",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", literally 'you'll lick your little fingers', is the Russian phrase for 'finger-licking good'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "пальчики",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is built from the normal word for fingers.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Надеюсь, это можно есть.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I hope this is edible.' The phrase for 'I hope', ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Надеюсь,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", shares a root with the name for hope. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "можно есть.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally means 'it is possible to eat', meaning edible.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Вы такого никогда не пробовали.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You have never tasted such a thing.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "никогда не пробовали.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " doubles the negative. After it, the describing word for 'such a thing' takes its 'of' form, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "такого",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Главное, чтобы было вкусно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The main thing is that it is tasty.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "чтобы",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'so that', and the action word after it goes into the past, as in ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "чтобы было вкусно.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Это не то обычное месиво.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'This is not that usual slop.' The expression for 'slop', ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "месиво.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", is built from the action word to knead. The describing word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "обычное",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " matches its shape.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Ладно, неси скорее на стол!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Alright, bring it quickly to the table!' The action word for carry while walking gives us its command to one person, ",
